description:
Design a secure data adapter that manages the flow of data packets between an incoming and outgoing interface. The module ensures that when data is valid and the outgoing interface is ready, it propagates the incoming data and control signals (such as start and end of packet markers). It also includes a mechanism to suppress any data from channels exceeding a predetermined maximum channel value, thereby preventing unauthorized or unwanted channels from being processed. This ensures operation within specified channel limits while maintaining synchronization between the input and output signals, with the added functionality of printing a message to indicate channel violations.
module top_module(

      // Interface: clk
      input              clk,
      // Interface: reset
      input              reset_n,
      // Interface: in
      output reg         in_ready,
      input              in_valid,
      input      [ 7: 0] in_data,
