description:
Design a sequential circuit that captures a single-bit input D on the rising edge of a clock signal CLK and produces an output Q. The output Q is the stored value of D, while an internal register reg2 alternates between its previous value and its complement on each clock cycle, effectively toggling its value. This module can function as a simple state buffer, maintaining the state of D and providing continuous output based on that stored value.
module top_module(
    input  D,
    output reg Q,  // Changed here to reg
    input  CLK
);

code:
module top_module(
    input  D,
    output reg Q,  // Changed here to reg
    input  CLK
);reg reg1 = 0;
    reg reg2 = 1;

    always @(posedge CLK) begin
        reg1 <= D;
    end

    always @(posedge CLK) begin
        reg2 <= reg1;
    end

    always @(posedge CLK) begin
        Q <= reg1;   // Q needs to be of type reg to be assigned
        reg2 <= ~reg2;
    end

endmodule

