Design a circuit that implements an asynchronous reset functionality for a synchronous input signal. When the reset signal is asserted, the output is driven LOW regardless of the synchronous input. Once the reset is deasserted, the output follows the synchronous input signal, capturing its value on the rising edge of the reset. This design ensures that the output signal reliably transitions to a defined state in response to an asynchronous reset condition.
module top_module(
  input reset,
  input sync_in,
  output sync_out
);

