description:
Design a circuit that converts a single grayscale input into multiple color channel outputs. The module takes an 8-bit grayscale value and duplicates it across a specified number of color channels, effectively replicating the grayscale input for each channel. This allows for uniform representation of the grayscale value across all defined channels, which is useful in applications requiring consistent color representation derived from grayscale data.
module top_module(
	gray,
	channels
    );

code:
module top_module(
	gray,
	channels
    );parameter color_width = 8;
	parameter color_channels = 3; 

	input[color_width - 1 : 0] gray;
	output[color_channels * color_width - 1 : 0] channels;

	genvar i;
	generate
		`define h (i + 1) * color_width - 1
		`define l i * color_width
		for (i = 0; i < color_channels; i = i + 1) begin: channel
			assign channels[`h : `l] = gray;
		end
		`undef h
		`undef l

	endgenerate

endmodule

